    "text": "Initially, a beaker has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of water at temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. Later another <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of water at temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> was poured into the beaker. The temperature, <math><mi>T</mi></math> of the water (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>)&nbsp;after mixing is"
